        // On the original contract, forward reverts iff the low-level call returned false.
        // The mutant inverts that behavior, so here we assert that reverted == true implies the call failed
        // but since we cannot observe the low-level success directly, we express the intended invariant:
        // For all inputs, reverted must equal the negation of the low-level call's success. However,
        // the only observable difference between original and mutant is that the original reverts when
        // the callee call returns false, so we assert that reverted implies the callee call would have failed
        // by performing the call externally and checking its success. That external call is allowed here
        // because it does not change c's state.
        (bool success, ) = callee.call(data);
        assert(reverted == !success);
    }
    receive() external payable { }
